  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building to upgrade the livestock value chain in Ethiopia, phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Ethiopia (GoE) has identified the livestock sector as a pivotal element in its 10-Year Perspective Development Plan - Ethiopia 2030: The Pathways to Prosperity (TYDP). This strategic focus recognizes the significant potential of livestock development to drive agricultural growth, enhance food security, generate employment, and support industrialization. Comprehensive strategies have been devised to modernize and transform the sector, aligning with the ambitious targets of the 2030 Agenda, the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2020-2025 for Ethiopia, and the Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) for Ethiopia.  Livestock production is a key component of the agricultural economy of Ethiopia and makes the country in the first rank in Africa in terms of population size. Ethiopia is among the largest live animal and meat exporters in Africa, mainly to the Middle East and North African countries. However, Ethiopia#s international market share is less than 1 per cent of the global meat trade. The main challenges include meeting the stringent international quality and safety standards in the competitive global markets and the presence of trade-sensitive transboundary animal diseases. Improving the production performance, sanitary and phytosanitary standards (SPS) a</narrative>
  </description>
